---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Privacy — Quran Reader">
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Privacy</h1>
  <div class="mt-6 flex flex-col gap-4 leading-relaxed">
    <p>Quran Reader has no accounts, no analytics and no tracking.</p>
    <p>
      Highlights, notes, bookmarks and reading position are stored in a local SQLite file on your device.
      They never leave it unless you export them yourself. Translations you import stay on your device too.
    </p>
    <p>
      The app goes online for one thing: when it starts, it asks GitHub Releases whether a newer version
      exists, and downloads it only if you choose to install it. GitHub sees that request like any
      download (your IP address, the app's version). You can turn the check off in the settings.
    </p>
    <p>
      “Report a problem” and the links in the credits open in your browser. A problem report is a
      form on GitHub with the verse and the app version filled in; nothing is sent until you submit
      it there.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
